<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Privacy Policy — LongDL Chrome Extension</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Privacy policy for the LongDL Chrome extension (DeepL Pro Unlimited – Longer Translations)." />
    <style>
      :root {
        --text: #1a1a1a;
        --muted: #555;
        --border: #e2e2e2;
        --bg: #ffffff;
        --accent: #0f62fe;
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body {
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto,
          Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
        color: var(--text);
        background: var(--bg);
        line-height: 1.6;
        max-width: 760px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 48px 24px 96px;
      }
      h1 { font-size: 30px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
      h2 { font-size: 20px; margin: 36px 0 12px; }
      h3 { font-size: 16px; margin: 24px 0 8px; }
      p, li { font-size: 15.5px; }
      ul { padding-left: 20px; }
      li { margin: 6px 0; }
      .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 32px; }
      .callout {
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 16px 20px;
        background: #fafafa;
        margin: 20px 0;
      }
      table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        margin: 12px 0 24px;
        font-size: 14.5px;
      }
      th, td {
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        padding: 8px 12px;
        text-align: left;
        vertical-align: top;
      }
      th { background: #f5f5f5; font-weight: 600; }
      a { color: var(--accent); }
      code {
        background: #f3f3f3;
        padding: 2px 6px;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-size: 13px;
      }
      footer {
        margin-top: 64px;
        padding-top: 24px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
        font-size: 13px;
        color: var(--muted);
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">
      LongDL — Chrome Extension "DeepL Pro Unlimited – Longer Translations"<br />
      Last updated: 4 May 2026
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Short version:</strong> The extension does not collect, store, or
      transmit any text you translate, your name, your email address, your IP
      address, or any browsing history. If you opt in, an anonymous random
      identifier and basic feature-usage events are sent to PostHog (EU servers)
      so we can see which features are used. You can opt out at any time in the
      extension's settings.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      This extension is provided by <strong>LongDL</strong> (the "Provider"),
      operating from Switzerland. For any privacy-related questions or
      requests, contact:
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Email:</strong>
      <a href="mailto:business.promptin@gmail.com">business.promptin@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      LongDL is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by DeepL SE.
      "DeepL" is a trademark of DeepL SE.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What the extension does</h2>
    <p>
      The extension splits long text submitted to deepl.com into smaller chunks
      and submits them sequentially through the DeepL web interface, allowing
      translation of texts that exceed DeepL's free-tier character limit. All
      translation work happens on deepl.com itself; the extension automates
      interactions with that page.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Data the extension processes locally</h2>
    <p>
      The extension stores the following data <strong>only on your device</strong>
      using Chrome's local storage. None of it is transmitted to the Provider or
      any third party:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Translation history, if you choose to keep it (managed via the History tab)</li>
      <li>Documents you upload for translation (processed locally and discarded after the translation completes)</li>
      <li>Loop and document-translation checkpoints, so a translation can resume after interruption</li>
      <li>Your settings and preferences</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can clear all locally stored data at any time by removing the
      extension from Chrome.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Optional anonymous analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The extension can send anonymous usage data to help the Provider
      understand which features are useful and which are not.
      <strong>Analytics are off by default.</strong> When you first install the
      extension, a dialog asks for your consent. You can change your choice at
      any time in the extension's settings.
    </p>

    <h3>4.1 What is collected (only with your consent)</h3>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Feature events</td>
          <td>
            Popup opened, tab switched, translation started/completed/failed,
            document upload, copy-to-clipboard, magic-fix used, swap used,
            settings opened.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Translation metadata</td>
          <td>
            Length category of the input ("0–500", "500–2k", "2k–5k", "5k–10k",
            "10k–25k", "25k+"), number of chunks, duration in milliseconds,
            error type if applicable.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Technical context</td>
          <td>
            Extension version, browser language (e.g. "de-CH"), an anonymous
            random identifier (UUID) generated on first opt-in.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>4.2 What is never collected</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The text you translate (input or output)</li>
      <li>The contents of any document you upload</li>
      <li>Your name, email address, or any account information</li>
      <li>Your IP address (IP geolocation is disabled in PostHog)</li>
      <li>Your browsing history or any data from sites other than deepl.com that the extension interacts with</li>
      <li>Your DeepL account credentials or session cookies</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>4.3 Where the data is processed</h3>
    <p>
      Anonymous analytics events are processed by
      <strong>PostHog</strong>, a product analytics service operated by
      PostHog, Inc. The Provider uses PostHog's
      <strong>EU Cloud</strong> instance, which stores data on servers located
      in the European Union (Frankfurt, Germany). PostHog acts as a data
      processor on behalf of the Provider. PostHog's privacy policy is available
      at <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://posthog.com/privacy</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>4.4 Legal basis</h3>
    <p>
      Processing of analytics data is based on your explicit consent
      (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR; Art. 31(1) Swiss FADP). You can withdraw your consent
      at any time, with effect for the future, by toggling the analytics switch
      in the extension's settings.
    </p>

    <h3>4.5 Retention</h3>
    <p>
      Analytics events are retained by PostHog for up to 12 months, after which
      they are automatically deleted. The anonymous identifier is reset if you
      uninstall the extension or revoke consent.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR and the Swiss FADP, you have the right to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Withdraw your consent for analytics at any time, without giving reasons (toggle in extension settings)</li>
      <li>Request information about whether analytics data associated with your anonymous identifier exists, and request its deletion</li>
      <li>Lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority — for users in Switzerland, the
        <a href="https://www.edoeb.admin.ch/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC)</a>;
        for EU users, your national data protection authority</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Because the analytics identifier is randomly generated and not linked to
      any account, the Provider cannot connect events to a specific person
      without you sharing your identifier. To exercise rights related to
      specific data, please include your anonymous identifier (visible in the
      extension's settings page) in your request.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Network requests made by the extension</h2>
    <p>
      The extension makes network requests only to the following destinations:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>deepl.com</code> — to perform translations (this is the core function)</li>
      <li><code>eu.i.posthog.com</code> — only if you have opted in to analytics, and only for sending anonymous usage events</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Children</h2>
    <p>
      The extension is not directed at children under 13. The Provider does not
      knowingly collect data from children.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      The Provider may update this policy from time to time, for example to
      reflect changes to features or legal requirements. Material changes will
      be communicated through the extension itself (e.g. a new consent prompt)
      or in the extension's release notes. The "Last updated" date at the top of
      this page indicates when the policy was last revised.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For any questions about this policy or your data, contact:
      <a href="mailto:business.promptin@gmail.com">business.promptin@gmail.com</a>
    </p>

    <footer>
      © LongDL · This policy is provided in English. The English version is
      authoritative.
    </footer>
